  "voice": {
    "post_text": [
      "1 year ago today we opened the doors to our little bakery in South End. It was a wild ride getting her opened and it's been just as wild since. But we have loved being able to connect with you in a more meaningful way through our little retail space!\n\nWhile the snow did ruin our original celebration plans...we thought why don't we just extend the party?! So our birthday cake flavored latte and croissant will be available all week long with a fun celebration planned on Saturday the 7th (more details to come)!\n\nThank you for supporting our little dream! You keep showing up day in and day out and we can't thank you enough. 🥂",
      "We made it! Come celebrate with us all week long!! 🥳\n\nOn Saturday the 31st we're throwing a big party to celebrate. @pertinaciouscoffee will be there with almond croissant lattes!!! We will have birthday cake croissants and fun specials for the day. It's going to be a party!!!\n\nThanks for one full year of our little bakery and cheers to many more. 🥂🥂🥂\n\n#charlottebakery #charlotte #entrepreneurlife #smallbusinessowners #smallbusiness",
      "Please enjoy this very chaotic day in the life! \n\nSometimes folks ask us why we moved away from pop ups as our sole business focus, and this is why!! Markets make you really dependent on good, reliable weather. Something that CLT does not have all the time. 😅 However, even the crazy ones can turn out great like it did on Saturday so I'm glad we still have markets on our schedule. \n\nThis year we will be back at the @southendmarketclt every third Saturday of the month! We're looking forward to reconnecting with our vendor community and getting to connect with you all! Also don't worry about keeping track. We're updating our online event page with all our pop up/market events and we always share ahead of time on our socials. \n...\n#dayinmylifevlog #smallbusiness #smallbusinessowners #farmersmarket #bakery",
      "Over the past three years I've made this exact same video and it's always so wild to watch. Sometimes it's hard to see our growth in the day to day mundane. It's especially hard when sales weren't quite where they needed to be all year long. \n\nBut this was such a huuuge big step of a year for us. At the start of 2025 I had one employee and now I have 5! Our bakery was waiting on one final inspection and now we're nearing the one year mark. 🥹 Sales were up 33% year over year and our foot traffic almost doubled. \n\nWe're really really thankful for you. Every single purchase you made helped keep this small business alive this year! I appreciate you showing up with kindness and excitement day after day. We really feel like we have some of the best customers in the world. 💞 \n\nWe're still dreaming/scheming about what 2026 will look like. But for sure we'll be making delicious pastries for the city we love. 🥐\n\nLots of love from the whole Wheatberry team. Cheers to 2026! 🥂\n\n#charlottebakery #bakery #2025reels #charlotte #charlottecake",
      "Friends tomorrow is the day! \n\n@el.veneno.clt/@themangomatcha will be hanging at the bakery from 8AM till they sell out with breakfast tacos and matcha! We also teamed up on two pastry specials that I seriously am so pumped about. We've made a lot but it's always a good idea to come early so you don't miss out!!\n\nAl Pastor Croissants 🌮\nKimmy's black al pastor, Oaxaca cheese, roasted pineapple all stuffed into our croissant and topped with cilantro \n\nDulce de Calabaza Danish 🎃\nCandied pumpkin with a piloncillo custard infused with baking spices",
      "introducing our newest wholesale account... @hilltopcoffee_ !!!\n\nWe were so excited to connect with Joy and her team as it's finally time for us to start growing our wholesale program again! With their location we're also so excited to reach a whole new part of Charlotte through this partnership. \n\nIf you haven't been to Hilltop Coffee yet their cozy cafe is super convenient for both Mallard Creek residents and University folks! I love how thoughtful the design of the space is and the coffee is so good. Such a necessary addition to a very underserved community. \n\nThey are currently selling our morning buns, ham croissants, everything danish and cookies. With hopefully more to come soon!",
      "The French Onion Croissant has been our team's favorite October special. Onions caramelized and deglazed with balsamic vinegar get rolled up and smothered in gruyere before baking. A little fresh chive to finish and you've got a super savory pull-a-part pastry. \n\nJust one more week to try this before we switch to November specials! We're open normal hours next week so come visit us Tuesday though Saturday 8-2PM. \n...\n#charlottebakery #charlotte #charlottefood #clteats #croissant #savoryfood",
      "So happy with how this custom request came out! We love incorporating color when we can so don't hesitate to ask (but keep in mind that with natural dyes we can't get deep/dark colors on the cake)!\n\nWith our vanilla whole wheat cake, peach jam and salted honey buttercream this was one last taste of summer in September. \n...\n#charlottebakery #cakes #cakedesign #charlotte #charlottecake #bakery #bakeshop",
      "Follow me along on a very early morning bake!\n\n#charlottebakery #ditl #businessowner #entrepreneurlife #smallbusiness #smallbusinessowners #bakery #bakerlife",
      "the buttermilk peach cruffin \n\ntangy buttermilk custard and sweet peach jam all stuffed into a sugar coated cruffin. we've loved this July special but she is about to retire so swing by soon to try one!!\n\n##charlottebakery #bakery #charlotte #cruffin #croissant"
